{"id":"CVE-2016-0772","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2016-09-02T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T22:30:04.119Z","description":"The smtplib library in CPython (aka Python) before 2.7.12, 3.x before 3.4.5, and 3.5.x before 3.5.2 does not return an error when StartTLS fails, which might allow man-in-the-middle attackers to bypass the TLS protections by leveraging a network position between the client and the registry to block the StartTLS command, aka a \"StartTLS stripping attack.\"","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://hg.python.org/cpython/rev/d590114c2394","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.splunk.com/view/SP-CAAAPUE","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2016-1630.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2016:1630"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2016-1627.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2016:1627"},{"url":"https://hg.python.org/cpython/rev/b3ce713fb9be","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2016-1629.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2016:1629"},{"url":"http://www.splunk.com/view/SP-CAAAPSV","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2019/02/msg00011.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20190207 [SECURITY] [DLA 1663-1] python3.4 security update"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1303647","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://docs.python.org/3.4/whatsnew/changelog.html#python-3-4-5","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2016/06/14/9","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20160614 Python CVE-2016-0772: smtplib StartTLS stripping attack"},{"url":"https://hg.python.org/cpytho